            <ArticleTitle>Sudden cardiac death in young children with neurofibromatosis type 1.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>718-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1) can manifest a characteristic vasculopathy that in adults is rarely associated with fatal coronary artery occlusion. We describe the clinical and pathological findings from 2 unrelated young children with NF1, a similar vasculopathy affecting their coronary arteries, and sudden cardiac death.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
